    {
      "id": "tripwire-and-reserve",
      "cardSha256": "ad43d29ddd9a989bd30953abbf620a93e866ec9bbc566906e696b115fd348dae",
      "side": "german",
      "name": "Tripwire and reserve",
      "idea": "Each platoon keeps part of its strength back by its stairwell, out of sight or nearly so, to fire at the Russians who get in: two squads and the 9-1 in F6, a squad and the 8-0 in J5, a squad in L7. The other squads watch the streets from level 1 with the machine guns.",
      "givesUp": "Four of the nine squads in the three large buildings do not fire as the Russians cross; the forward squads fight alone until the reserve comes up, and the squad at L7 has no leader.",
      "terrain": [
        "H5 sees G5, H4, I5, and I6 at range 1 and F4 and I4 at 2; of the Russian setup Locations only E4 (range 3), G4 (range 2), and J2 (range 4) see it.",
        "F6, the F5 building's stairwell hex, has no LOS to or from any Russian setup Location.",
        "K4 sees J3, K3, L3, and L4 at range 1; J4 sees H4 at range 2, G5 at 3, and F4 at 4; J5, the K5 building's other stairwell hex, is seen from G4 at range 3, from level 2 of G3 and from N5 at 4, and from E4 at 5.",
        "L6 sees L5, K6, and M6 at range 1 and L4 and N6 at 2; L7 at ground level has no LOS to or from any Russian setup Location.",
        "I7 and M9 are one-hex stone buildings with a ground level only; F5, K5, and M7 have levels 1 and 2, reached by the stairwells in F6, J5, K4, and L6."
      ],
