    {
      "id": "fire-first",
      "cardSha256": "ad43d29ddd9a989bd30953abbf620a93e866ec9bbc566906e696b115fd348dae",
      "side": "russian",
      "answers": {
        "plan": "forward-line",
        "placementsSha256": "02b0096f5b42765e21eab239c618da9273a2ff5a790ae7a2d41fe42bac2536bc"
      },
      "name": "Fire first",
      "idea": "The German forward line stands in the Guards' LOS at range 2, and the Russians move first. Nine Guards squads on the upper floor of E4, F3, and G4, with the 10-2 at F3, fire on the F5 platoon in the first Prep Fire Phase; three squads wait unseen at G3 to cross once it breaks. The 308th fires from the upper floor of M5 and N5 on K4, K5, L6, and M7 at range 2.",
      "givesUp": "The nine squads that fire do not move in the first turn, and they stand in the LOS of the German squads they fire on; only three squads are fresh for the first crossing.",
      "terrain": [
        "E4 and F3 see F5 at range 2; G4 sees F5, G6, and H5 at range 2. A 6-2-8 fires at full strength to range 2.",
        "G3 at ground level is seen from no German setup Location.",
        "M5 sees K4 and K5 at range 2, and L6 and M7 at range 2; N5 sees L6 and M7 at range 2.",
        "J2, M2, and N2 are one-hex buildings with a ground level only, so their groups have no choice of hex; N2 is seen from no German setup Location.",
        "The stacks at G3 and N2 are out of every German LOS, so each may take a \"?\" once both sides have set up (A12.12)."
      ],
